  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The equiatomic Cr-Mn-Fe-Co-Ni alloy has lower effective stacking-fault energy than the equiatomic Cr-Fe-Co-Ni and Cr-Co-Ni subsets.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lower stacking-fault energy of Cr-Mn-Fe-Co-Ni results from its enhanced chemical complexity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower stacking-fault energy promotes deformation twinning.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC5314382::web::008::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stacking-fault-energy variation changes the balance between dislocation slip and deformation twinning.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changes in twinning and slip behavior cause differences in yield strength and strain hardening.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC5314382::web::008::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanical-property differences are independent of the mere number of constituent elements.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The target quinary, quaternary, and ternary alloys can all be prepared as single-phase FCC materials.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The compared alloys have comparable grain size, texture, and initial defect density after identical thermomechanical processing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weak-beam dark-field TEM measurements of dislocation splitting can be used to quantify stacking-fault energy in these alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The controlled comparison will use room-temperature uniaxial tensile deformation with identical strain rates, processing histories, grain-size distributions, and textures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical twins impede dislocation motion and thereby affect work hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5314382::web::008::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The equiatomic Cr-Fe-Co-Ni and Cr-Co-Ni alloys have higher stacking-fault energies than the quinary baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the quinary alloy, the quaternary and ternary alloys will show lower deformation-twin density and more slip-dominated deformation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the quinary alloy, the quaternary and ternary alloys may have lower yield strength or altered strain-hardening rates.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower stacking-fault energy, greater twin activity, and the quinary alloy's modified mechanical response should correlate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC5314382::web::008::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quinary baseline is characterized by low stacking-fault energy and pronounced deformation twinning.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5793551::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Other chemistry-dependent effects, including lattice distortion, magnetic effects, or compositional fluctuations, may also influence the mechanical-property differences.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8875034::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Statistically indistinguishable stacking-fault energies and twin densities across the three alloys, or a lack of correlation with mechanical behavior, would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
